mod:param_redef_store_guards;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 2: DEF-685, seat D2's D5, stacked on row 1). A STORE THROUGH A POINTER PARAMETER THE CALLEE REDEFINED LANDS
// WHERE THE PARAMETER NOW POINTS, not in the argument first passed (`a = b; (<-a).lp = v`). The escape analysis walks a MARKED parameter's own
// chain (where the body pointed it) BESIDE main's record of the store at the parameter, never in its place, so the callee's summary records the
// store and the caller's view across the call is refused. A parameter is marked only on three roads: (1) it is assigned whole (`a = b`, in one
// branch too); (2) refs land on its own address ref (`rp = @r; <-rp = p2`); (3) `@o` or `$$ o`, under casts too, is handed to a callee whose
// summary stores refs through that parameter (`bothp(@o, o, p2, hq)`). An address taken alone (`rdhp(@p)`) marks nothing.
// THE GUARDS (6, one per form, one cell each): `a4_shat`, `a4_fldat`, `a4_nrlat`, `a4_wrat`, `a4_slfdat`, `a4_dfat`. Main (acb78ea), row 1 and
// this row refuse each at the same site; D4 as it stood (the walk of a marked parameter's chain IN PLACE OF main's record, and `@p` alone marking
// `p`) accepted each and read freed heap (236 at -O0 and -O2, 97 under the detector). They guard against that either/or coming back: a store
// reached through a struct local after `rdpp(@p)` (`a4_shat`), two hops from a struct local (`a4_fldat`), the no-root branch (`a4_nrlat`), the
// write alone with no value stored (`a4_wrat`), a slice parameter (`a4_slfdat`), and `@p` taken in a `defer` (`a4_dfat`).
// THE MUTANTS' KILLERS (3, this row's step 5): `k_pa7_r1`, `k_slfdat_r1`, `k_sl7`. Main, row 1 and this row refuse each at the same site; the
// mutant each names in its comment, which brings the either/or back for a parameter marked by a real road, accepted it and read freed heap.
error:E5;
struct:K_a4_shat = { int64:k; };
struct:H_a4_shat = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K_a4_shat:kk; };
func:mk_a4_shat = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh_a4_shat = H_a4_shat() never fails { pass H_a4_shat{ l: raw mk_a4_shat(), k: 2i64, kk: K_a4_shat{ k: 3i64 } }; };
func:growh_a4_shat = int64(H_a4_shat->:w_a4_shat) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w_a4_shat.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
